---
title: Boozy (Just Slightly) Cherry Cheesecake
servings: 6
course: Dessert
locale: en
difficulty: Medium
---

= Cheesecake Base =

Mix the @unsalted butter{55%g}(melted) with the @digestive biscuit crumbs{180%g} and press into the bottom of an #8” springform pan{}. Chill in the refrigerator for ~{10%minutes}.

Mix together the @cream cheese{450%g}(e.g. Primula), @mascarpone{100%g}, @soured cream{80%g}, and @caster sugar{200%g} in a large bowl until smooth and well-combined. Stir in the @eggs{3%large} one at a time, then add the @vanilla extract{1%tsp}.

Sift the @flour{30%g} and @salt{0.5%tsp} into the batter, folding it in until combined. Pour the cake batter into the tin on top of the crumb crust.

Preheat the oven to 150°C. Bake the cheesecake for ~{1%hour}.

Cool the cheesecake at room temperature, then refrigerate it for at least ~{6%hours}.

= Cherry Topping =

Mix the @cornflour{1%tbsp} with 1 tbsp @amaretto{2%tbsp} to form a paste.

Simmer the @frozen pitted cherries{400%g} in a saucepan with @caster sugar{2%tbsp}, the other 1 tbsp amaretto, and @water{60%ml} for 5 to ~{6%minutes}.

Stir whilst slowly adding the cornstarch paste into the cherries. Simmer for 3 to ~{4%minutes}, until thickened. Remove the cherries from the heat and wait for them to cool to room temperature.

Remove the cheesecake base from the tin, and top with the cherries.

> The cheesecake will keep refrigerated for up to 3 days.